{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ledgerly",
    "_postman_id": "9f3c2b41-0d5e-4a77-9d1c-6b8e2f0a4c11",
    "description": "Ledgerly - a toy bank ledger that stays correct under concurrent load.\n\n**Run the folders in order** (Accounts -> Transfers -> Reconciliation -> Error cases), or hit Run collection: the first request captures the seeded account ids into collection variables that everything else depends on.\n\nStart the app with `./gradlew bootRun` (defaults to http://localhost:8080). If you changed the port, edit the `baseUrl` collection variable.\n\nDemo path for an interview:\n1. `List accounts` - note the balances and the `version` field.\n2. `Transfer money` - money moves, one transferId returned.\n3. `Replay the same request` - identical response, nothing appended to the ledger.\n4. `List transfer events` - exactly two new rows, one DEBIT and one CREDIT.\n5. `Reconcile the ledger` - every balance re-derived from the log, debits equal credits.\n\nFor the concurrency story run `./gradlew test` (200 concurrent transfers over 4 accounts), then hit `Reconcile` and look at `retriesAbsorbed`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Accounts",
      "description": "Account projections. Balances here are a cached view; the event log is the source of truth.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List accounts (paginated)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts?page=0&size=20&sort=id,asc",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "accounts"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "0"
                },
                {
                  "key": "size",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "id,asc"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Paginated list of accounts as DTOs. Run this first: it captures the seeded account ids into collection variables that every other request uses."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const page = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('page has content', () => pm.expect(page.content).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty);",
                  "",
                  "// Seed the ids the rest of the collection transfers between.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('fromAccountId', page.content[0].id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('toAccountId', page.content[1].id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('fromAccountBalance', page.content[0].balance);",
                  "",
                  "console.log('from=' + page.content[0].id + ' to=' + page.content[1].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Open a new account",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "accounts"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates an account. The opening balance is written to the event log as an OPENING event in the same transaction, which is what lets /reconcile derive this account's balance from history alone.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Eve\",\n  \"openingBalance\": \"640.00\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('returns a Location header', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "",
                  "const a = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('newAccountId', a.id);",
                  "pm.test('opens with the requested balance', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(Number(a.balance)).to.eql(640));",
                  "pm.test('starts at version 0', () => pm.expect(a.version).to.eql(0));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
